//RS /// D-FACT-LAW1=B: every row states which way is safe and which written words
//RS /// move it the other way; a row with no meaningful direction states none, and a
//RS /// row that states neither fails the build. This is the law-zero drift guard
//RS /// extended — one implementation in `Registry::law_violations`, not a second
//RS /// guard per kind.
